meta-commands:
  :help            this message
  :quit            leave the REPL (Ctrl-D does the same)
  :clear           clear the screen
  :vars            list the bindings of this session
  :type EXPR       evaluate EXPR and print the type of the result
  :ast EXPR        print the syntax tree of EXPR without running it
  :disasm EXPR     print the bytecode EXPR compiles to, without running it
  :time EXPR       evaluate EXPR and report how long it took
  :load PATH       run a file in this session
  :reset           forget every binding and start over
  :cancel          throw away the input being typed at the `...` prompt

EXPR may be any statement. A line that does not start with `:` is
Jaithon: bindings persist, and a bare expression prints its value.
